# Blueprint CMS – building history

## 2026-10-25 – First task: routing content

- Dependencies: notrab/dumbo (HTTP/PSR-7, router), illuminate/support (Collection, Arr), michelf/php-markdown,
  symfony/yaml (front matter – not in the spec, but needed to parse yaml), pestphp/pest (dev).
- Fixed public/index.php: PROJECT_DIR is now dirname(__DIR__), autoload path pointed outside the project.
- Config: Config::load($dir) reads config.php + config.{hostname}.php (hostname sanitized, port stripped).
  App::create() adds site/config as fallback, so the project config/ (deployment) overrides site/config (project code).
- Routing: Dumbo only gets one catch-all route; content resolution happens in Site::find(). Dumbo's trailing-slash
  removal is disabled, because the canonical url depends on the content: pages with published subpages end with "/"
  (/blog -> /blog/), all others don't (/imprint/ -> /imprint). /home redirects to /. Query strings are kept.
- Pages: folder page (page.json, page.md, page.content.md, page.php) or file page ({slug}.md / {slug}.php).
  File pages are only .md/.php, which keeps site.json, users.json and redirects.json from becoming pages.
  "NN_" prefix = sort number (listed page), "." prefix = draft. Folder pages win over file pages with the same slug.
- page.php semantics (spec only showed an example that echoes + exits): it is the page's own renderer, executed at
  render time only (never while scanning, because it may have side effects). Returning an array instead merges the
  array into the page data and renders the normal template.
- Data: nested maps -> Data objects (page()->data()->some->nested), lists -> arrays, missing keys -> null, so templates
  don't fail on optional fields. Values are raw; escaping is the template's job (esc()).
- Drafts are only resolved when User::current() is set. Sessions are only started if the client sends a session
  cookie, so anonymous visitors don't get sessions. Panel login doesn't exist yet.
- redirect() throws a Redirect exception, so it works from any depth of template/partial code.
- Spec mentions both site/templates/snippets/ (folder structure) and partials (helper) – went with
  site/templates/partials/ as the helper describes.
- Errors: debug=true shows class/message/file/trace, otherwise a plain 500 page; 404 uses site/templates/404.php.
- Tests: Pest against the real content/ (routing spec) plus tests/fixtures/project for page.php,
  redirect(), config merging and slug collisions (the real content/01_blog/page.php calls exit()).

2026-10-25 – Blueprints
- Followed Kirby v6/develop (src/Blueprint/Normalizer.php): root `fields` are definitions as soon as there is a
  layout (tabs/columns/sections); tabs and columns reference them by name. Every blueprint is normalized into
  tabs -> columns -> fields (loose fields -> one 1/1 column, loose columns -> `main` tab). Legacy sections are
  converted to fields (pages -> pagelist, files -> filelist, fields section -> its fields), groups are spliced.
  Unreferenced definitions are ignored, like in Kirby.
- Split: Blueprint (loading, lookup, accessors, validation), BlueprintNormalizer (pure array transformation,
  gets a `find` closure for `extends`), Field (one field definition). The user asked for Blueprint\Field as the
  name of the definition class, so the planned per-model value object ($page->createdAt()) needs another
  name (e.g. FieldValue).
- Invalid fields (unknown type, missing reference, duplicate name, missing extends) become red `info` fields
  instead of exceptions, so one typo doesn't break the panel view (Kirby behaviour).
- Deviations from Kirby: `title: text` (string that is a field type) sets the type instead of extending; a list
  of references can contain inline definitions (`- text: {type: textarea}`); `title: true` with an existing
  root definition uses that definition. Labels: "seoTitle" -> "Seo title".
- Lookup: site/blueprints/{name}.{yml,yaml,php}, then core blueprints in src/blueprints/ (pages/default, site,
  users/default, files/default). Page blueprint: pages/{template} -> page blueprint with `default: true`
  (from the user's example page.yml) -> pages/default. User blueprint: users/{role} -> users/default.
- Raw blueprint files are cached by absolute path (static), so tests with different projects don't collide.
- Validation (required, min/max, minlength/maxlength, pattern, email/url/date/time, static options, nested
  structure/object rows) is part of the blueprint, since blueprints are the data structure definition.
- options/status normalization per model type, no i18n yet.
- Planned (user note): every blueprint field becomes a model method returning a formatted, escaped value object
  ($page->createdAt(), ->isEmpty(), ->format()); raw values stay in $page->data(). Conflicts with existing Page
  methods (title(), url(), template(), …) need to be resolved then.
- Docs in docs/ (guides, reference, examples), structured as a content folder (NN_folder/page.md with a title in
  the front matter), so the CMS can render them with contentFolder=docs. Links point to page.md files (GitHub).

2026-10-25 – User blueprint fallback, field methods
- User role defaults to "user"; blueprint lookup users/{role} -> users/user -> users/default (core).
- Field methods: HasFields trait (Page, Site, User, Values) with __call -> FieldValue. Model methods win over field
  names (PHP only calls __call for undefined methods), field("url") is the escape hatch. Page::title() now returns a
  FieldValue (falls back to the slug) – breaking, but consistent.
- FieldValue echo = formatted by type + escaped. Exceptions: textarea renders markdown with no_markup (inline html
  escaped, md() stays the raw variant), writer/list output their html as is (trusted editor content).
  password/structure/object/blocks/layout output nothing.
- Unknown methods are passed to illuminate/support: Carbon (date/time), Collection (lists), Stringable (rest).
  String results are wrapped in a FieldValue again so chaining never leaks unescaped output; empty values return an
  empty FieldValue so ->format() etc. don't fail. esc(FieldValue) returns it unchanged (no double escaping).
- List entries get a single-value type (tags -> select etc.), structure rows and objects become Values.
- Normalized blueprints are cached per file (static), since each page asks its blueprint for field definitions.

2026-10-25 – Panel
- User requirements: Kirby-like minimal UI (left sidebar + main view), Vue components, form fields as simple and
  native as possible, behind a login at /panel, communication via REST API, page rendering independent of the panel.
- Backend: Panel class with its own small regex route table (page ids contain slashes, so ids use "+" like Kirby:
  /panel/api/pages/blog+newest_entry). App's catch-all route now accepts all methods and only hands /panel to the
  panel when `panel` is enabled; with panel=false, /panel is a normal page path and non-GET requests get 405.
- Auth: password_hash in users.json, session cookie (HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax), session id regenerated on login, a
  CSRF token per session required as X-CSRF-Token header for changes. No sign up/installer: users are created with
  bin/blueprint (avoids an unauthenticated "create first admin" endpoint). Failed logins are delayed slightly.
- Saving: only blueprint fields that store a value are taken from the request, merged with the existing data and
  validated by the blueprint (422 with errors per field path); other data in the file stays. Empty values remove the
  key. Folder pages write page.md if it exists, otherwise page.json; page.content.md keeps the `content`.
  {slug}.php pages are read-only.
- Status = folder name: draft ".slug", unlisted "slug", listed "NN_slug" (appended after the last listed sibling,
  two digits like the existing content). New pages are always drafts. changeNum renumbers listed siblings.
- Frontend: Vue 3 + vue-router + Vite in panel/, built into public/panel/ (gitignored, `composer panel:build`).
  Native inputs (date/datetime-local/time/number/color/select/radio/checkbox/select multiple/textarea), native
  <dialog> for dialogs (no window.confirm). Structure rows as fieldsets with up/down/remove, tags as comma
  separated text with a datalist. Files, blocks and layout have no editor yet. Dark mode via prefers-color-scheme.
- structuredClone fails on Vue proxies -> JSON clone helper (all values are JSON anyway).

2026-10-25 – Files, blocks, layouts, sorting, slugs, uids, page types
- Page type (user request, like Kirby's intendedTemplate): `type` in the page data (default "page") chooses the
  blueprint pages/{type}.yml and the template templates/{type}.php -> page.php -> default.php. Replaces the
  `template` key (content and fixtures migrated). The pagelist filter option keeps Kirby's name `template`
  (`type` is the field type).
- UIDs: 10 chars [a-z0-9] (like the existing user uid). Added on every write (page update/create, file meta,
  users), `bin/blueprint content:uids` backfills. Pickers store references page://uid, file://uid, user://uid,
  so references survive slug changes; old values (paths, filenames, emails) are still resolved.
- `fields: true` in a tab/column = all definitions not used elsewhere, in definition order (first such column).
- Files: everything else in a page folder; .md/.php are subpages, so they (and executable/server config
  extensions) can't be files. Meta in {filename}.json (a json file whose name minus .json exists is meta).
  Served under the page url by App when no page matches; only images/media/pdf/text inline, everything else as
  download, plus nosniff + CSP sandbox (no html/svg execution on the site/panel origin). Site files are not
  supported (content/ root holds site.json, users.json, ... – too easy to expose).
- Uploads: raw request body (POST /pages/{id}/files?filename=…), no multipart parsing; names sanitized;
  file blueprint `accept` (mime/extension/maxsize) checked after the meta (template) is written.
- Blocks/layout: Kirby content format. Fieldsets normalized in the normalizer (list, map with inline/extended
  definitions, groups), core block types in src/blueprints/blocks + snippets in src/views/blocks, overridable in
  site/. Recursive block types are stopped with an error fieldset. Validation per visible block.
- Panel: native HTML5 drag & drop (sortable.js, handles for items with inputs, nested lists independent), page
  tree in the sidebar (expand state in localStorage), slug/type dialog, file view, filelist/filepicker, blocks
  and layout editors. Block content is edited in place inside the view's reactive values.

2026-10-25 – Sorting files
- Files are sorted by `sort` in their meta data (then filename). Page::sortFiles(filenames) numbers the given
  files 1..n and keeps the rest after them, only changed meta files are written. API: PATCH /pages/{id}/files
  {"sort": [...]}. Filtered file lists move a file to its target's position in the full list.
- site/blueprints/pages/page.yml: 2/3 column with all other fields (`fields: true`) + 1/3 column with a filelist.

2026-10-25 – Roles
- Roles = `user` + the user blueprints (site/blueprints/users/*.yml without default). Creating/updating a user
  only accepts those; the current role stays valid when its blueprint is gone (no lockout by deleting a file).
  Panel: RoleInput is a select, or just the role's title when `user` is the only role. No built-in admin role.

2026-10-25 – File links in textareas, only used files are public
- Panel: files dragged from a file list (custom drag type with the file's data) or from the computer (uploaded
  first) onto a textarea insert `![name](file.jpg)` / `[name](file.pdf)` at the caret; other pages' files with
  their path (`blog/file.jpg`). Sortable lists now use a custom drag type instead of text/plain, so inputs don't
  get the item index inserted when something is dropped on them.
- Relative links are stored (portable when slugs change), File::resolveUrls() turns `hello.jpg` /
  `blog/hello.jpg` in rendered markdown into the file url (textarea field values and md()).
- File::isUsed(): filename (with word boundaries) in the own page's data, or `file://uid` / `page/id/file`
  in any page's or the site's data. Unused files are 404 for visitors, visible for logged in users (panel
  previews). The check scans all pages only for files that aren't used on their own page.

2026-10-25 – Image optimizer
- Ported from minimaxcms (user's project): AVIF in public/media/images/{sha256(file hash|maxFileSize|quality)}.avif,
  auto quality by resolution, quality then resolution reduction to reach maxFileSize, temp file + rename.
- Differences: sources are File objects (resolved from urls, paths, file://uid or filenames of the current page via
  App::resolveFile()), only used files are converted (the optimizer must not make unused files public), the
  helpers return raw urls (escape in templates, like all helpers). `optimizeContentImages` (default false) runs
  optimized_content_images() over every rendered page; the helpers work without it. bin/blueprint media:clear.
- The 2x3 test png was hand-made and not decodable (getimagesize only reads the header): replaced by a GD png.

2026-10-25 – Storage format
- Page::contentFormat() / changeContentFormat(): json (page.json, recommended), md (page.md front matter + text),
  json+md (page.json + page.content.md). New files are written before the old ones are removed; single file pages
  (`about.md`) become folders. Panel: "Storage format" in the page settings dialog (renamed from "Slug and type").
- Structural page changes (move/rename, convert, create, delete) now refresh App's cached page tree themselves,
  not only the panel API.

2026-10-25 – File context menu
- File lists have a context menu (right click or the ⋯ button): Open, Rename, Change position, Replace, Delete.
  `ContextMenu.vue` is a generic teleported menu (items + "-" separators, keyboard navigation, closes on outside
  click, wheel, Escape, window blur/resize; not on scroll events, focusing the menu can scroll the document).
- Replace: `PUT /panel/api/pages/{id}/files/{filename}?filename=…` with the raw body, same extension required.
  `File::replace()` moves the old file to a hidden backup and restores it if the new one fails the `accept` rules,
  so filename, uid, data and all references stay. Files expose `modified` (mtime), thumbnails use it as cache buster.

2026-10-25 – Optimized image urls with the original filename
- `public/media/images/{hash}/{filename}.avif` instead of `{hash}.avif`: readable urls (and downloads) keep the
  image's name, the hash folder still makes them unique and cache-safe. `media:clear` deletes the hash folders.

2026-10-25 – Page ids with slashes in the panel
- Panel and API urls use the slug path (`/panel/pages/blog/newest_entry`, `/panel/api/pages/blog/newest_entry/files`)
  instead of Kirby's `+`: readable and identical to the page id. Routes with suffixes (`/children`, `/files`,
  `/files/{filename}`) come first with a non-greedy page id; the first matching path decides (other methods → 405,
  so `DELETE /pages/blog/files` never deletes a page). The slugs `children` and `files` are reserved in the panel.

2026-10-25 – createdAt and modifiedAt
- `SystemFields::apply()` fills `uid`, `createdAt` and `modifiedAt` (ISO 8601) on every write of pages, files and
  users, as the first keys of the data. Existing `uid`/`createdAt` win over written values, so they can't be changed.
  Not in blueprints or panel forms (hidden), but field methods treat the dates as `datetime` fields
  (`SystemFields::field()`) unless the blueprint defines a field with that name. Replacing a file updates its
  `modifiedAt`. Hand-written content without them gets them with the next write.
- The site gets `createdAt`/`modifiedAt` too (`SystemFields::applyDates()`, no uid). Blueprints can show the dates as
  read-only fields (`type: datetime, disabled: true`, examples in site/blueprints/site.yml and pages/page.yml);
  the panel API never saves `disabled` fields.

2026-10-25 – Content independent tests
- Tests never read the project's content/site folders (they change while working on the site): `createApp()` needs a
  project dir, the routing tests use the `tests/fixtures/website` fixture.

2026-10-26 – Kirby style snippets
- `snippet($name, $data, $return, $slots)` renders `site/snippets/{name}.php` like Kirby: lists of names (first
  existing), missing snippets render nothing, slots via `snippet(…, slots: true)` / `slot()` / `endslot()` /
  `endsnippet()` (`Snippet` keeps a stack of open snippets, output buffering; `$slot`, `$slots->name()`).
- `partial()` stays as it is (site/templates/partials, exception if missing).
- Block snippets moved from site/templates/blocks to site/snippets/blocks (Kirby location), core fallback src/views/blocks.

2026-10-26 – partial() returns the html
- `partial($name, $variables)` returns the html instead of echoing (`<?= partial("head") ?>`, no `$return` flag),
  throws if missing, and takes an absolute path to a php file instead of a name (IDEs can follow it).

2026-10-26 – Admin role and password confirmation
- Core blueprint `users/admin.yml` (extends `users/default`), so `admin` is always a role; `User::isAdmin()`.
- `PATCH /users/{uid}` with a `password` needs `currentPassword` (the logged in user's password, also when changing
  another user's password), admins are exempt. The panel's password dialog asks for it unless the user is an admin.
- Only admins choose or change roles (API 403, the panel hides the role select). The only user is always an admin
  (`User::role()`), the first created user gets the admin role, and creating a second user stores the admin role on
  the first one if needed, so there is always an admin.
- Non-admins only see and edit themselves: `GET /users` returns only the current user, other users' endpoints → 403,
  creating and deleting users is admin only. The panel hides the Users list for them (sidebar link, breadcrumb,
  /users redirects to the own account). Consequence: a userpicker of a non-admin only offers themselves.

2026-10-26 – Panel saves only changed fields
- `useEditing` sends only the fields that differ from the loaded values (cleared ones as null). The API already
  merged partial `data`, so concurrent edits of different fields no longer overwrite each other. No conflict
  detection for the same field (last save wins).

2026-10-26 – Conflict check with modifiedAt
- `PATCH` bodies can carry `modifiedAt` (from loading) and `original` (loaded values of the sent fields).
  `Panel::checkConflicts()`: if the stored `modifiedAt` differs, every sent field whose stored value differs from
  `original` is a conflict → 409 `{conflicts: [...]}`. So edits of other fields still merge, only real conflicts
  stop the save. The panel shows "Load their version" / "Overwrite with mine" (resend without `modifiedAt`).
- `modifiedAt`/`createdAt` now have milliseconds, saves within the same second must not look unchanged.

2026-10-26 – Docs as a website
- docs/ without sorting numbers: `name.md` pages, folders with `page.md` only for pages with subpages; the order is
  `sort` in the front matter (the menu sorts by it, then by title). Links are site paths (`/guides/content#files`),
  links to project files became plain code (they don't exist on the website).
- Rendered with `contentFolder` = docs: `site/snippets/layout.php` (a snippet with slots: header, collapsible site
  tree on the left, breadcrumb, previous/next, "On this page"), `site/templates/default.php` and `404.php` use it.
  `public/assets/docs.css` (Kirby docs like, dark mode, menu as drawer below 800px) and `docs.js` (heading ids +
  anchors, "On this page" with the current section, copy buttons, mobile menu). No syntax highlighting yet.
- Code highlighting for the docs only: `public/assets/js/highlight.js` (module, loaded by the docs layout) imports
  speed-highlight 2.1.0 from jsDelivr when a page has ```lang blocks, colors the `<code>` inline so our `<pre>`
  styles stay, github-light/-dark themes by color scheme. speed-highlight has no php, so a small own grammar is
  registered with `setLoader()`; `sh` → `bash` etc.

2026-10-26 – Snippets in site/templates/snippets
- Snippets (and block snippets) moved from `site/snippets/` to `site/templates/snippets/`, as in the original spec,
  next to `site/templates/partials/`.

2026-10-26 – CLI commands as files
- `bin/blueprint` only creates the app and calls `Cli::run($argv)`. Commands are php files returning
  `["command", "description", "usage"?, "run"]`: core ones in `src/cli/commands/`, own ones in `site/cli/`
  (same name overrides the core command). `run(array $args)` may return an int exit code (default 0), exceptions
  print the message and exit with 1. Unknown/no command prints the usage generated from all commands, site
  commands in an own "User defined commands:" section.
- `askPassword()` became `Cli::askPassword()`.

2026-10-26 – Page icons in the sidebar
- The page tree shows a house icon for the home page unless its blueprint sets `icon`; other pages show their blueprint's `icon` too (page summaries now contain `isHome`, `icon` falls back to `home` for the home page).
- `icon` is a panel icon name or any text (emoji), rendered by `PageIcon.vue`. The icon paths moved to `panel/src/icons.js`; `site` is now a globe so the house is unique to the home page.
- The icons are hand-written line paths (Feather/Lucide style, not copied), documented in the panel guide.

2026-10-26 – Moving pages, drafts and bulk actions
- `Page::changeParent(?Page)` moves a page (with subpages and files) into a folder page or the root; it keeps its status, listed pages get the next number of the new siblings. Not for the home page, not into itself or its subpages, not if the slug exists there. API: `PATCH /pages/{id}` with `parent`.
- The draft status can't be disabled by a blueprint anymore (`draft: false` is ignored), every page but the home page can be taken offline.
- Page tree: context menu (right click / ⋯) with "Move to …" and the statuses. Page settings: parent select (`ParentSelect.vue`). Page lists: checkboxes + select all, bulk status / move / delete (one request per page, failures are collected).
- The page view reloads after changes elsewhere (`session.changes`) when it has no unsaved changes; the tree follows the open page when it is moved.

2026-10-26 – Subpages as a default field
- The panel no longer injects a subpages list below the form: `Blueprint::DEFAULT_FIELDS` gives every page blueprint (and the site) a `subpages` field of type `pagelist`, in a full width column at the end of the first tab. It is skipped if the blueprint has a pagelist or a field named `subpages`; `subpages: false` turns it off. The type stays `pagelist` (no new `subpages` type).
- `false` removes any field, also inherited ones referenced by the layout (references to removed fields are skipped instead of becoming error fields).
- Pages rendered by a php file (no form) still get the subpages list below.
- The `site` icon is now an earth with land masses instead of a plain globe grid.

2026-10-26 – More panel icons, image icons
- The icon set grew to ~220 icons with the names of Kirby's panel icons (no brand logos), all hand-drawn in the existing line style. Generated from helpers (circles, rounded rects, gear) and reviewed on a contact sheet; `icons.js` keeps the plain path data.
- An icon is a stroke path or `{d, fill}` with a filled path (circle-filled, star-filled, status-*, grid-*).
- Blueprint `icon` also accepts `data:image/…` URIs (other data URIs are ignored). They are rendered as a CSS mask in the text color, so foreign svgs fit the theme and can't run scripts.

2026-10-26 – Panel icons in the docs
- The icon data moved to `panel/src/icons.json` (imported by `icons.js`), so the docs page `docs/reference/panel-icons` can read it: its `page.php` returns the text of `page.md` plus a grid of all icons, rendered with the docs template.

2026-10-26 – Docs search
- The docs header has a search field: a client side fuzzy search (Fuse.js 7.0.0 from jsDelivr) over the pages listed in `#docs-menu` (title, weighted higher, and the section path like "Reference › Blueprints"). "/" focuses it, arrow keys + Enter open a result, Escape closes. Without Fuse (offline) it falls back to a substring search. Full text search can come later.

2026-10-26 – House icon for the site
- The `site` icon (sidebar "Site") is the house again, like `home`; the earth drawing stays available as `earth`.

2026-10-26 – Docs logo
- `public/assets/images/blueprint_cms.svg` (the project logo) is the docs favicon and sits next to the site name in the docs header; on narrow screens only the logo is shown, the name stays for screen readers.

2026-10-26 – speed-highlight default theme
- The docs use speed-highlight's `atom-dark` theme in both color schemes instead of github-light/-dark, so code blocks are always dark (`--color-pre-*`, also the copy button).
- Back to speed-highlight's `dark` theme (instead of `atom-dark`). The logo uses a brighter blue.

2026-10-26 – Docs: panel link only for logged in users
- The "Edit in panel" link in the docs header is only shown when a user is logged in (and the panel is enabled) and opens the current page in the panel (`/panel/pages/{id}`, `/panel/site` without a page).

2026-10-26 – Panel: open page in the tree
- The sidebar tree highlights the open page (also while one of its files is open, `route.params.id`) and expands its parents (stored like manually expanded pages), then scrolls it into view.

2026-10-26 – Panel api subresources with ~, no system fields in markdown
- Subresources in the panel api and panel urls start with `~` (`/pages/{id}/~children`, `/pages/{id}/~files/{filename}`, `/site/~children`), which slugs cannot contain. The reserved slugs `children`/`files` are gone, a page may be called `files` (the docs page reference/blueprints/files was read as the file list of reference/blueprints).
- Markdown pages (`{slug}.md`, `page.md`) do not store `uid`, `createdAt`, `modifiedAt`: both dates come from the file modification time (PHP has no creation time); a `uid`/`createdAt` in the front matter written by hand is kept. `content:uids` skips them. Converting a page to `md` drops its uid (references fall back to the path).

2026-10-26 – Icon field
- New field type `icon`: an icon name (datalist of the panel icons), emoji/short text, or an uploaded svg up to 50 KB stored inline as `data:image/svg+xml;base64,…` (`Field::isValidIcon`, `IconField.vue`). The value of a page's first `icon` field overrides its blueprint's icon in the panel (`Panel::pageIcon`).
- The home page no longer gets a house icon by default, set it in its blueprint or icon field.

2026-10-26 – Markdown Extra as option
- `md()` and textarea fields use plain Markdown by default; config `"markdown" => ["extra" => true]` enables Markdown Extra (tables, footnotes, …). Both go through `App::markdown($markdown, $markup)`. The docs project enables it in `config/config.php`.

2026-10-26 – Writer field: markdown editor
- `writer` stores markdown now (no longer html like Kirby's writer) and is rendered like `textarea`: escaped inline html, resolved file links. Breaking for html content in writer fields.
- Panel: `WriterField.vue` uses tiny-markdown-editor (TinyMDE, exact version 0.2.34) for the live markdown highlighting, but not its command bar: its buttons are divs that only react to mousedown, so an own toolbar of native buttons (panel icons) calls TinyMDE's command api. Subtle styling in the panel's grays (markup dimmed), monospace font, no TinyMDE default css.
- Toggling bold/italic/strikethrough/code with the caret right before the closing marker steps over it, TinyMDE alone would remove the formatting and select the word.
- Links to pages are inserted as `[Title](page://uid)` (the url for pages without uid), chosen in `PageSelectDialog.vue` (browse level by level, search via `GET /pages?search=`); links to files of the page via `FileSelectDialog.vue`. Dropping files works as in textareas (shared `isFileDrag`/`droppedFileLinks` in files.js).
- `File::resolveUrls()` resolves `page://uid` and `file://uid` in markdown links to urls, so references in markdown survive renamed slugs.

2026-10-26 – Passkeys, accent color
- Panel login with passkeys (WebAuthn) besides email + password, if the browser supports them (`PublicKeyCredential` and `getPublicKey()`). Passkeys are discoverable (resident keys) with required user verification, so they replace both email and password.
- No library: new passkeys send their public key as SPKI (`getPublicKey()`) and no attestation is requested, so the server only checks the client data (type, one time challenge from the session, origin host = request host, https except on localhost) and the authenticator data (rp id hash, user present + verified flags, counter), logins are verified with `openssl_verify`. ES256 and RS256.
- Stored in the user's `passkeys` in users.json; the api only shows id, name and dates. Only the user can add passkeys to their account, the user and admins can delete them (user view).
- `--color-accent: #068ef5` for checkboxes, radios, switches and the focus color.

2026-10-26 – Accent colors: docs blue, panel black
- `#068ef5` is the accent of the docs (`--color-accent` in docs.css, light and dark), not the panel: the panel's `--color-accent` is its black primary color again, the focus color its blue again. The variable stays, so a project can set its own panel accent.
- Panel checkboxes and radios are drawn with css (`appearance: none`): accent background, check in `--color-accent-text`, rounded corners; Firefox showed its own blue ones before. Wrapped in `:where()`, so rules like `.item-select` keep their size and margins.

2026-10-26 – Field methods with a leading underscore
- `$page->_url()` returns the field value even if the model has a method with that name; `HasFields::__call` strips one leading underscore (same as `field("url")`).

2026-10-26 – Plugins, static site generator
- Plugins are folders in `site/plugins/` with an `index.php` or `{folder name}.php` (like Kirby, plus the named file). Only that entry file is loaded, when the app is created (after `App::instance()` is set), in alphabetical order; the plugin's other php code can live anywhere (`src/` by convention), the entry file requires it. No autoloader, no plugin registry api yet.
- A plugin can have `blueprints/`, `templates/` (snippets, partials, 404.php) and `cli/` like the site. Lookup order: site, plugins (alphabetical), core – one helper `App::siteDirs($folder)` used by templates, snippets, partials, the 404 template, `Blueprint::roots()` and `Cli`. Blueprints of plugins count as non-core for `Blueprint::forType()`.
- First plugin: `site/plugins/static-site-generator`, command `static:build [folder] [--clear-existing-target-folder]` (default `static/`, gitignored). It renders every listed and unlisted page through `App::request()`, so the output is exactly what the app serves (page php files, optimized images); pages become `{path}/index.html`, redirecting pages and `redirects.json` become meta refresh pages. Used page files are copied, `public/` without `index.php`, `panel/` and dot files, plus `404.html` (`App::notFoundResponse()` is public now, `Redirects::all()` new). An existing target folder is only replaced with the flag; the project folder, its parents and the content/site/public folders are always refused (paths are resolved without `..` and symlinks).

2026-10-26 – Release script
- `composer release [version]` → `bin/release`: suggests the next version after the latest `v*` tag (first `0.1.0-alpha.1`; pre-release: next number, the later stages of alpha → beta → rc, the release; release: patch, minor, major, next minor alpha.1) or takes an own version, strictly checked with semver.org's regex (a leading `v` is stripped), ordered by semver.org's precedence (`compareVersions()`)
- writes `version` after `name` into composer.json, panel/package.json and panel/package-lock.json (re-encoded with their indentation), refreshes composer.lock's content hash (`composer update --lock --no-install`), commits only these files (`git commit --only`, other staged changes stay staged) and creates an annotated tag `v{version}`; refuses when these files have uncommitted changes, no push
- no `phlak/semver`: the script only needs the regex, the precedence and a few increments (its parser also accepts `1.2`, and its patch increment turns `0.1.0-alpha.1` into `0.1.1` instead of `0.1.0`)

2026-10-26 – GitHub Actions, docs on GitHub Pages
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: Pest on PHP 8.3, 8.4, 8.5 (the versions Pest supports), plus the panel build (Node 24, `npm ci`)
- `.github/workflows/docs.yml`: on pushes to main, `bin/blueprint static:build _site` renders the docs (the repo's config uses `docs/` as content) and `actions/deploy-pages` publishes them to https://pstaender.github.io/blueprint-cms/
- GitHub Pages serves the project in a subfolder, so the static site generator got `--base-path=/blueprint-cms`: root-relative `href`/`src`/`action`/`poster` attributes and redirect urls get the prefix (a regex over the rendered html, no template changes); the workflow takes it from `actions/configure-pages` (empty with a custom domain)

2026-10-26 – Security: no html or script links from editors
- Any panel user (also the `user` role) could put scripts into the site: `md()` allowed inline html, markdown kept `javascript:` links, `list` fields were output as raw html, url/link fields weren't checked. The site and the panel share an origin, so such a script in an admin's browser could read the CSRF token and create an admin.
- `md()` / `App::markdown()` escape inline html by default, `md($text, html: true)` allows it for content panel users can't edit. Markdown links and images with schemes other than `Field::SAFE_URL_SCHEMES` (http, https, mailto, tel, page, file) or relative urls become `#` (`url_filter_func`); Markdown Extra's `{key=value}` attributes are already ignored without markup.
- `list` fields are rendered like `textarea` (markdown, escaped html). `url` and `link` field values with unsafe schemes are output as empty strings, `url` validation rejects them (`FILTER_VALIDATE_URL` accepts `javascript://…`).
- The docs page panel-icons renders its generated svg list itself after the markdown instead of appending html to the content.

2026-10-26 – Content Security Policy
- Rendered pages (also 404 and 500) get a `Content-Security-Policy` from the config `csp` (directive => sources, merged recursively, `false` removes a directive or the header) and `nosniff`. Default: only the site's own scripts, inline styles allowed (layout block), images `'self' data: https:`, media `'self' https:`, YouTube/Vimeo frames for the video block, `object-src 'none'`, `frame-ancestors 'self'`. `csp_nonce()` returns a per-request nonce, it's added to script-src only if a template used it.
- The docs (site/config/config.php) allow jsDelivr in script-src and style-src (Fuse.js, speed-highlight and its theme).
- Files that aren't in `File::INLINE_MIMES` are served as `application/octet-stream`: with `script-src 'self'` an uploaded file detected as javascript could otherwise be included by a `<script src>` (the sandbox csp of the file response doesn't apply to the including page).
- The panel shell sends `Panel::CSP` (no inline scripts, inline styles for Vue style bindings, `data:`/`blob:` images for icons and previews, `frame-ancestors 'none'` against clickjacking), API responses `default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'` and `nosniff`. Checked in headless Chrome: docs and panel (login, page editing, users) without violations.

2026-10-26 – Blueprint as a composer package
- `composer.json` has `"bin": ["bin/blueprint"]`, so websites get `vendor/bin/blueprint`. The script loads `$_composer_autoload_path` (set by composer's bin proxy) or its own `vendor/autoload.php`; the project dir is the root package's `install_path` (`Composer\InstalledVersions`), which is the website when installed as a dependency and the repository itself otherwise, also with a custom `vendor-dir`.
- The built panel is part of the release instead of a build step in every website (no Node.js needed there): `public/panel/` is no longer gitignored, `composer release` runs `npm ci` + `npm run build` and commits `public/panel/` with the version files (Vite's content hashes keep unchanged builds identical). Composer installs tags from GitHub's archive, so the panel has to be committed.
- `bin/blueprint public:build [--force]` (`PublicFolder`) copies `index.php`, `.htaccess` and `panel/` from the package's `public/` into the website's `public/`. The panel is replaced (old hashed assets removed), `index.php`/`.htaccess` are kept unless `--force` since websites may customize them; fails if the package's panel isn't built; a no-op in the repository itself. No `panel:build` cli command for websites: the package doesn't contain node_modules and websites shouldn't need Node.js.
- `public/.htaccess` rewrites everything that isn't a file or folder to `index.php` (Apache). The static site generator already skips dot files.
- `.gitattributes` leaves the repository's own project (docs, `config/`, `site/`, `public/assets/`), the panel sources, tests and dev files out of the package (`export-ignore`, GitHub's tag archive is what composer downloads); `public/index.php`, `.htaccess` and `public/panel/` stay in it.

2026-10-26 – Symfony VarDumper
- `dd()` and `dump()` come from `symfony/var-dumper` (a runtime dependency, templates use them): collapsible html dumps in the browser, colored output in the cli, `->dump()`/`->dd()` of collections work too. Composer loads the dependency's functions first, so symfony's `dd()` wins (unlike the own one it doesn't discard the output buffers, html rendered before the `dd()` call is sent too). The own `dd()` (var_dump in `<pre>`) stays as a fallback and `Dumper` is only registered when the VarDumper class exists: a website that symlinks the package into its vendor folder without installing its new dependencies would otherwise fail at `App::create`. The dump's inline script isn't blocked by the CSP, since `dd()` exits before the response headers are sent.
- `symfony/var-dumper: *` (the version illuminate/support works with). `Dumper` (registered in `App::create`) gives the html dumps an own light/dark theme (css variables, `prefers-color-scheme`) instead of Symfony's dark one, the cli keeps the `CliDumper`.
